Naqoyqatsi is a 2002 American non-narrative film directed by Godfrey Reggio
and edited by Jon Kane, with music composed by Philip Glass.

11
01:09:55,714 --> 01:10:01,714
It is the third and final installment in the Qatsi trilogy.

12
01:16:17,142 --> 01:16:23,142
The title comes from the Hopi word naqö̀yqatsi meaning "life of war".

13
01:22:38,571 --> 01:22:44,571
In the film's closing credits, the title is also translated as
"civilized violence" and "a life of killing each other".
